{"h":2857,"lines":[{"y":0.057138970883326423,"c":1,"w":0.071645075480143205,"h":0.015960204843210146,"t":"Reading","x":0.84217348662984004},{"h":0.018927897165670893,"x":0.19204152150704271,"y":0.10461861442833265,"t":"Then there is the risk of disease. In 2015, an outbreak of haemorrhagic septicaemia,","w":0.69204152425130216,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"caused by the normally harmless bacterium Pasteurella multocida, killed over 75% of","x":0.19204151897937863,"y":0.12351294588104167,"w":0.6989619445800781,"h":0.017494751574527623},{"t":"the global adult saiga population in just three weeks. In 2017, 60% of the Mongolian","w":0.6989619445800781,"c":1,"y":0.14098837212115689,"x":0.1903114151488749,"h":0.018913657453362043},{"x":0.19031142723529484,"w":0.7179930623372397,"c":1,"h":0.017513060252761559,"t":"saiga population - a subspecies found nowhere else in the world - was killed by a virus","y":0.15988372064826439},{"t":"that spilled over from livestock. These so-called mass mortality events represent an","h":0.01961094687417142,"c":1,"y":0.17718249876377279,"w":0.68523590087890629,"x":0.19025304266762968},{"y":0.1976744183205722,"w":0.39446367899576829,"x":0.19204151682400863,"c":1,"t":"unpredictable and serious threat to the species.","h":0.017511026103484872},{"t":"Climate change poses a further threat. Although well adapted to cold winters and","x":0.19204151517374196,"w":0.67474049886067711,"h":0.01744186102384615,"y":0.23255813925285995,"c":1},{"x":0.19204152406919434,"w":0.68512110392252601,"c":1,"t":"hot summers, saiga struggle to cope with temperature extremes and unpredictable","h":0.017615790797581132,"y":0.2514534880903323},{"c":1,"t":"tluctuations in climate. Experts believe that unusually warm weather may have","y":0.27034883692745981,"x":0.19031142985813471,"w":0.64186848958333331,"h":0.017614773722942956},{"h":0.019067245066958449,"w":0.63667821248372392,"t":"triggered the 2015 mass mortality event. The steppe region has also become","x":0.19031141267415638,"y":0.28779069770190735,"c":1},{"x":0.19031143109979562,"h":0.01744186102384615,"c":1,"y":0.30668604622973517,"w":0.67301035563151035,"t":"increasingly arid in recent years, and many of the smaller streams that the species"},{"y":0.32400279948176292,"w":0.42733566284179686,"c":1,"t":"normally depended on have dried up and vanished.","x":0.19204151106325579,"h":0.019020456296735322},{"c":1,"t":"Recent efforts to save the saiga have been spearheaded by the Altyn Dala","x":0.19204151264596192,"y":0.3603918822578458,"w":0.61245676676432292,"h":0.018968582820692248},{"w":0.65224914550781254,"h":0.018969599895330536,"t":"Conservation Initiative, a project led by the Association for the Conservation of","c":1,"x":0.19204151712521772,"y":0.37928621402459117},{"x":0.1920415251693216,"y":0.39678096547409503,"c":1,"h":0.018916708677277239,"t":"Biodiversity of Kazakhstan, working in partnership with the Kazakh government's","w":0.66262975056966145},{"h":0.018917725751915526,"y":0.41567529723666596,"x":0.1920415332128681,"c":1,"t":"Committee for Forestry and Wildlife, Frankfurt Zoological Society and Fauna and Flora,","w":0.71799306233723958},{"y":0.43456962892281548,"t":"an international conservation charity. Its purpose is to protect and restore Kazakhstan's","h":0.017494751574527623,"x":0.1903114157848817,"w":0.71453287760416662,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"steppe, semi-desert and desert ecosystems and the many species they support,","x":0.19031143047463048,"y":0.45346396068389894,"w":0.65743942260742183,"h":0.017494751574527734},{"x":0.18846740616174393,"w":0.69569549560546873,"y":0.46943941865381478,"h":0.023091184750897997,"c":1,"t":"including the critically endangered saiga. In 2022 the United Nations recognised the"},{"t":"initiative as a World Restoration Flagship project, an accolade reserved for the ten best","h":0.018921794050468899,"y":0.48982558142402155,"w":0.71799306233723947,"c":1,"x":0.19031142721891475},{"c":1,"x":0.19031141156530965,"w":0.53633219401041665,"t":"examples of large-scale ecosystem restoration around the globe.","y":0.50872092994991469,"h":0.017521197517240239},{"y":0.5450581395633981,"h":0.018972651119245509,"c":1,"w":0.71626296997070327,"t":"So, how many saiga are there now? By 2000, the global saiga population had hit an all-","x":0.19031142149374838},{"w":0.70588236490885414,"h":0.019025542337298806,"c":1,"x":0.19031141262342752,"t":"time low of just 21,000 individuals. There was some recovery in the first decade of the","y":0.56250000002826184},{"w":0.69387552897135418,"h":0.019796472900476036,"t":"new millennium but this was then crushed by devastating mass mortality events that","c":1,"x":0.19025686401907818,"y":0.58082235216726386},{"t":"saw the loss of hundreds of thousands of the species. But thanks to the intervention","h":0.017608671275112786,"y":0.59867039876346662,"c":1,"w":0.69204152425130205,"x":0.18858131406093909},{"t":"of the Altyn Dala Conservation Initiative, the most recent episodes in the ongoing","w":0.67301035563151035,"x":0.19031143109288035,"h":0.019063176101033252,"c":1,"y":0.61756473084212382},{"y":0.63558103624060713,"t":"story of the saiga have been relatively uplifting. Three years ago, the Ustyurt Plateau","x":0.19025118600606788,"w":0.69561233520507804,"h":0.020445273087690397,"c":1},{"x":0.19031140882803849,"h":0.017611722499027871,"c":1,"y":0.6553533940568036,"t":"population in Kazakhstan experienced its largest mass birth of saiga calves in many","w":0.68166091918945315},{"t":"years. An aerial census two years ago recorded an estimated 842,000 saiga across","h":0.01761273957366627,"y":0.67424772581920045,"w":0.67647059122721342,"c":1,"x":0.18858131329284647},{"w":0.6799307759602865,"h":0.017559848355612973,"c":1,"t":"Kazakhstan as a whole, and according to an aerial survey earlier this year, the saiga","y":0.69174247750284634,"x":0.19031142854006569},{"c":1,"h":0.01756086543025126,"t":"population in Kazakhstan now exceeds 1.9 million. The world's strangest-looking","w":0.66262975056966145,"x":0.19031142220926892,"y":0.71063680926519779},{"x":0.19031142667367609,"y":0.72813156059032924,"t":"antelope remains critically endangered, but the direction of travel is positive.","h":0.018961462630851855,"c":1,"w":0.63321797688802084},{"t":"61","c":1,"h":0.01308139510051276,"y":0.95784883727895875,"x":0.8858131489939145,"w":0.020761245091756142}],"w":2400}